+	// routes. A packet spawned when only res->rt exists is unroutable to the
+	// sink (the router can't reach it) -> it waits. The moment rt->host is
+	// drawn the table rebuilds and the packet forwards via the FRESH table +
+	// delivers. A spawn-time-cached route would have stayed "unroutable"
+	// forever; the per-hop model re-evaluates at every step.
